{{!
    @template assignsubmission_refchecker/export_pdf_reference

    One reference's block in the downloadable report. Rendered once per reference, so that a long
    reference list does not go through TCPDF's HTML parser as a single enormous string.

    This template is rendered into TCPDF's writeHTML(), NOT into a browser. TCPDF understands only
    a small fixed subset of HTML and loads no stylesheet, so classes do nothing here: use inline
    style attributes, and only color, background-color, font-size, font-weight, text-align, border
    and width. There is no flexbox, grid or float, so any columns must be a table with an explicit
    percentage width on every cell, because TCPDF's automatic widths are unreliable.

    One exception to "style everything with CSS": cellpadding is read by TCPDF only as an
    attribute (tcpdf.php getHtmlDomArray), so it stays an attribute here even though HTML5 calls it
    obsolete and the Mustache linter says so.

    All values other than the admin authored strings come from external databases, so this template
    uses HTML escaping variables throughout and never triple-brace ones.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * heading string - "Reference 1"
    * rawref string - the reference exactly as the student wrote it
    * matchstatuslabel string - the localised match status
    * statuscolor string - the hex colour for that status
    * hasconfidence bool - whether a confidence score applies
    * matchconfidence int - the confidence score, 0-100
    * confidencelabel string - the label for the confidence score
    * retracted bool - whether the matched work has been retracted
    * retractedwarning string - the retraction warning
    * predatory bool - whether the journal is possibly predatory
    * predatorywarning string - the predatory journal warning
    * haserror bool - whether this reference failed to check
    * errormessage string - why it failed
    * hasdetails bool - whether anything was matched
    * details array - the matched metadata, as label and value pairs
    * hasissues bool - whether any issues were reported
    * issueslabel string - the heading for the issues list
    * issues array - the issue strings

    Example context (json):
    {
        "heading": "Reference 1",
        "rawref": "Smith, J. (2019). Learning at scale. Nature, 570(7760), 12-15.",
        "matchstatuslabel": "Verified",
        "statuscolor": "#146c43",
        "hasconfidence": true,
        "matchconfidence": 94,
        "confidencelabel": "Confidence",
        "retracted": false,
        "retractedwarning": "",
        "predatory": false,
        "predatorywarning": "",
        "haserror": false,
        "errormessage": "",
        "hasdetails": true,
        "details": [
            {"label": "Title", "value": "Learning at scale"},
            {"label": "Year", "value": "2019"}
        ],
        "hasissues": false,
        "issueslabel": "Issues",
        "issues": []
    }
}}
<p style="font-size: 10pt;">
    <span style="font-weight: bold;">{{heading}}</span>
    <span style="color: {{statuscolor}}; font-weight: bold;">&nbsp;&nbsp;{{matchstatuslabel}}</span>
    {{#hasconfidence}}
        <span style="color: #5c636a; font-size: 8pt;">&nbsp;&nbsp;{{confidencelabel}} {{matchconfidence}}%</span>
    {{/hasconfidence}}
</p>

<table cellpadding="4">
    <tr>
        <td style="width: 100%; border: 0.5px solid #adb5bd; background-color: #f8f9fa; font-size: 9pt;">{{rawref}}</td>
    </tr>
</table>

{{#retracted}}
    <p style="color: #b02a37; font-weight: bold; font-size: 9pt;">{{retractedwarning}}</p>
{{/retracted}}

{{#predatory}}
    <p style="color: #997404; font-weight: bold; font-size: 9pt;">{{predatorywarning}}</p>
{{/predatory}}

{{#haserror}}
    <p style="color: #5c636a; font-size: 9pt;">{{errormessage}}</p>
{{/haserror}}

{{#hasdetails}}
    <table cellpadding="2">
        {{#details}}
            <tr>
                <td style="width: 22%; font-size: 9pt; color: #5c636a;">{{label}}</td>
                <td style="width: 78%; font-size: 9pt;">{{value}}</td>
            </tr>
        {{/details}}
    </table>
{{/hasdetails}}

{{#hasissues}}
    <p style="font-size: 9pt; font-weight: bold;">{{issueslabel}}</p>
    <ul style="font-size: 9pt;">
        {{#issues}}<li>{{.}}</li>{{/issues}}
    </ul>
{{/hasissues}}

<br>
